# System Scope Document

## 1. Purpose

The purpose of this document is to define the scope and boundaries of the Secure Approval-Centric System developed as part of the Software Engineering project. This document outlines what the system will include and what it will not include.

---

## 2. Project Overview

The Secure Approval-Centric System is a web-based application designed to manage approval workflows in a structured and secure manner. The system allows users to submit requests and authorized personnel to approve or reject those requests while maintaining proper tracking and security.

---

## 3. Stakeholders

* End Users (Requesters)
* Approvers (Authorities)
* Project Team Members
* Course Instructor

---

## 4. System Features (In Scope)

The system will include the following features:

1. User Registration and Login (Role-Based Access)
2. Secure Authentication using JWT
3. Request Submission Form
4. Approval and Rejection Workflow
5. Request Status Tracking
6. Basic Activity Logging
7. Logout Functionality

---

## 5. Out of Scope

The system will NOT include:

* Payment processing
* Advanced analytics dashboard
* Mobile application
* Integration with external APIs
* Multi-level complex workflow engine

---

## 6. Assumptions

* The system will be used in a controlled academic environment.
* Users will have basic knowledge of web applications.
* The system will be deployed locally or on a basic cloud platform.

---

## 7. Constraints

* Development will follow Agile methodology.
* Effort estimation will be done using the COCOMO model.
* Version control will be managed using GitHub.
* Project tracking will be managed using Jira.

---

